From d72d9939bc7c3257e98d295448a0bd710cf47683 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Roessner <c@roessner.co>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 14:45:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] milter: expose local DSN origin evidence

Expose the local-MTA marker and versioned original envelope through normal Milter macro negotiation. Values exist only for notifications that bounce(8) submits with trusted transient cleanup state.

Document configuration, record format, consumer validation, and the use of the normal cleanup service and non_smtpd_milters setting.
---
 README_FILES/MILTER_README   | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 html/MILTER_README.html      | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 proto/MILTER_README.html     | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/cleanup/cleanup_milter.c | 10 ++++++++++
 4 files changed, 117 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/README_FILES/MILTER_README b/README_FILES/MILTER_README
index aafc693..b679996 100644
--- a/README_FILES/MILTER_README
+++ b/README_FILES/MILTER_README
@@ -279,6 +279,37 @@ non_smtpd_milters, header_checks or body_checks (lines 3-5 below).
     4     header_checks = don't reject internally-generated bounces
     5     body_checks = don't reject internally-generated bounces
 
++LLooccaall--MMTTAA eevviiddeennccee ffoorr ddeelliivveerryy ssttaattuuss nnoottiiffiiccaattiioonnss
+
+A Milter cannot determine from message content whether a delivery status
+notification was generated by the local Postfix MTA. When bounce filtering is
+enabled as shown above, Postfix therefore makes the following macros available
+for delivery status notifications generated by bounce(8):
+
+{postfix_dsn_evidence}
+    The constant value postfix-dsn-evidence-v1. This value indicates that
+    bounce(8) obtained the original-envelope information from the original
+    Postfix queue file and passed it to the normal cleanup(8) service.
+{postfix_dsn_original_envelope}
+    An unpadded base64url encoding of the original envelope. The decoded,
+    network-byte-order record contains: one version octet with value 1; a two-
+    octet sender length and the sender bytes; a two-octet recipient count; and,
+    for each recipient recorded in the original queue file, a two-octet length
+    and the recipient bytes.
+These macro values are transient cleanup(8) state. They are not obtained from
+message headers or body content, and are not stored in the new queue file. A
+Milter that authenticates a local delivery status notification must require
+both macros, reject an unknown record version or malformed encoding, and obtain
+delivery action and status information from the RFC 3464 message/delivery-
+status body part.
+
+A Milter can request these macro names through normal Milter macro-list
+negotiation. Otherwise, specify them in an appropriate Postfix Milter macro
+parameter such as milter_end_of_header_macros. Milters that do not request the
+names are unaffected. The normal cleanup(8) service and the normal
+non_smtpd_milters setting are used; no Milter protocol extension or separate
+cleanup service is required.
+
