+<h4> Local-MTA evidence for delivery status notifications </h4>
+
+<p> A Milter cannot determine from message content whether a delivery
+status notification was generated by the local Postfix MTA.  When bounce
+filtering is enabled as shown above, Postfix therefore makes the following
+macros available for delivery status notifications generated by <a href="bounce.8.html">bounce(8)</a>:
+</p>
+
+<dl compact>
+
+<dt> <tt>{postfix_dsn_evidence}</tt> </dt> <dd> The constant value
+<tt>postfix-dsn-evidence-v1</tt>.  This value indicates that <a href="bounce.8.html">bounce(8)</a>
+obtained the original-envelope information from the original Postfix queue
+file and passed it to the normal <a href="cleanup.8.html">cleanup(8)</a> service. </dd>
+
+<dt> <tt>{postfix_dsn_original_envelope}</tt> </dt> <dd> An unpadded
+base64url encoding of the original envelope.  The decoded, network-byte-order
+record contains: one version octet with value 1; a two-octet sender length
+and the sender bytes; a two-octet recipient count; and, for each recipient
+recorded in the original queue file, a two-octet length and the recipient
+bytes. </dd>
+
+</dl>
+
+<p> These macro values are transient <a href="cleanup.8.html">cleanup(8)</a> state. They are not obtained
+from message headers or body content, and are not stored in the new queue
+file. A Milter that authenticates a local delivery status notification must
+require both macros, reject an unknown record version or malformed encoding,
+and obtain delivery action and status information from the <a href="https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc3464">RFC 3464</a>
+<tt>message/delivery-status</tt> body part. </p>
+
+<p> A Milter can request these macro names through normal Milter macro-list
+negotiation. Otherwise, specify them in an appropriate Postfix Milter macro
+parameter such as <a href="postconf.5.html#milter_end_of_header_macros">milter_end_of_header_macros</a>. Milters that do not request
+the names are unaffected. The normal <a href="cleanup.8.html">cleanup(8)</a> service and the normal
+<a href="postconf.5.html#non_smtpd_milters">non_smtpd_milters</a> setting are used; no Milter protocol extension or separate
+cleanup service is required. </p>
+
